.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-6i3cya/TASK-260720-6i3cya_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:4616:.task-board/.resources/STORY-260720-35dck7/STORY-260720-35dck7_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:6224:TASK-260720-17llva,task,go-v1-manager-profile,Specify the normative go-v1 manager lifecycle,backlog,STORY-260720-35dck7,,"Extend the manager profile with the complete closed go-v1 execution and installation lifecycle. The manager must validate and audit immutable source before any compiler work, derive all process arguments and output paths, isolate toolchain state, keep private builds outside shared commit locks, and publish only verified immutable artifacts through a manager-home transaction.","Work in curator-spec origin/main commit 57c1f56846d221ecc55786bd3c2467ec32f11730. Own profiles/manager.md only. Specify trusted Go 1.23 plus allowlisted families, curator-go-toolchain-v1, private telemetry-off initialization, the clean environment, native vendor-only target, fixed direct argv for telemetry, version, env, list, and build, dependency and directive rejection, cache trust and receipts, currentness, status, repair, rollback, recovery, lock ordering, consumer-last commit, and locked GC. CLI wording and schemas are separate tasks.","The profile states source validation, context exclusion, build-source digest, closure and collisions, source audit and registry gates before cache lookup or compilation; all five Go argv forms and the fixed environment are normative and no shell or package-selected executable or argument can enter the process graph; go list checks every active dependency and embed input, rejects native files, syso, non-standard assembly, cgo, go:cgo_import_dynamic, path escapes, unknown toolchains, workspaces, downloads, PGO, and external-link fallback; dry-run never runs go list or go build and leaves all listed persistent paths unchanged; real installs build misses before mutation, then use deterministic project and manager-home lock ordering, protected cache publication, one journal, reverse rollback, consumer last, recovery, repair, and GC; build failure preserves prior installation byte-for-byte; python3 tools/validate.py passes.","[""TASK-260720-1nvomm""]","[""TASK-260720-12iigs""]","[{""text"":""Specify the five fixed Go argv forms, clean environment, and allowed process graph exactly"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Specify audit-before-build, compiler-free dry-run, locked commit, rollback, recovery, repair, and GC ordering"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Run the scoped profile validation command and record the result"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T01:44:31Z,2026-07-20T01:54:45Z,true,[],"[{""name"":""TASK-260720-17llva_install-lifecycle.puml"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-17llva/TASK-260720-17llva_install-lifecycle.puml"",""description"":""Normative install and dry-run activity model for manager-profile implementation""}]","[{""name"":""TASK-260720-17llva_install-lifecycle.svg"",""uri"":""file://TASK-260720-17llva/TASK-260720-17llva_install-lifecycle.svg"",""description"":""Rendered lifecycle diagram linked to the manager-profile task""}]"
.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-6i3cya/TASK-260720-6i3cya_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:4617:.task-board/.resources/STORY-260720-35dck7/STORY-260720-35dck7_spawn-log_-analyst--solution-architect--codex-.log:6226:TASK-260720-1s1vr6,task,build-driver-conformance-vectors,Generate go-v1 build-driver conformance vectors,backlog,STORY-260720-35dck7,,"Add a separate minimal Go build skill fixture and generated build-driver vectors that are implementation-neutral. Cover the accepted valid declaration and every security-relevant rejection at the manifest, filesystem, toolchain, dependency graph, compiler directive, process, cache, and context boundaries.","Work in curator-spec after the schema-case generator task. Own a new separate Go fixture below conformance/v1/fixtures, its expected context and identity artifacts, new conformance/v1/vectors/build-drivers.json, and the corresponding generator functions and tests in tools/generate-vectors. Keep the existing script golden fixture and registry hashes unchanged. Include a transitive embedded input and vendored dependency variant. Do not add shared transaction lifecycle scenarios here.","Positive vectors cover schema 6 build_roots, mixed script and build commands, build-source exclusion while unrelated context remains visible, valid vendor-only main package, exact curator-build-source-v1 and curator-go-toolchain-v1 bytes, CCJ-1 build input and cache key, canonical receipt bytes and hash, derived artifact path, all five direct Go argv forms, fixed environment, cache hit, and compiler-free dry-run miss; negative vectors cover schema 5, unknown driver and forbidden fields, missing unused overlapping or runtime-overlapping roots, root or escaped source, links and special files, nested module, non-main or multiple package, missing or inconsistent vendor data, workspace or toolchain switching, unsupported Go family, cgo and native inputs, syso, assembly includes, escaped embed inputs, go:cgo_import_dynamic, generators, PGO, poisoned environment and fake Go, telemetry failure, external-link or libgcc fallback, toolchain path and digest failures, cache key or target or receipt or artifact corruption, noncanonical receipt, concurrent publisher, forged self-consistent receipt outside protected state, and marker-embed build-source regression; cache-hit and dry-run context vectors run no source-aware Go commands; generation is deterministic, go test ./tools/generate-vectors passes, and the existing script fixture expected hashes remain unchanged.","[""TASK-260720-37ei85""]","[""TASK-260720-cw39jh""]","[{""text"":""Generate the separate Go build fixture and all positive identity, context, process, cache, and dry-run vectors"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Cover every minimum rejection cluster from the accepted research contract with named expected outcomes"",""done"":false},{""text"":""Prove existing script-fixture and registry expected hashes are unchanged and regeneration is deterministic"",""done"":false}]",,2026-07-20T01:44:32Z,2026-07-20T01:49:31Z,true,[],[],[]
