L-stream structural-collision regression; toolchain vectors exercise unsorted files, directories and internal links, LF and CRLF version normalization, mode and timestamp non-inputs, malformed version output, invalid Unicode, duplicate paths, escaping links, a selected executable outside GOROOT, and tree mutation; negative vectors cover schema 5, unknown driver and forbidden fields, missing unused overlapping or runtime-overlapping roots, root or escaped source, links and special files, nested module, non-main or multiple package, missing or inconsistent vendor data, workspace or toolchain switching, unsupported Go family, cgo and native inputs, syso, assembly includes, escaped embed inputs, go:cgo_import_dynamic, generators, PGO, poisoned environment and fake Go, telemetry failure, external-link or libgcc fallback, toolchain path and digest failures, cache key or target or receipt or artifact corruption, noncanonical receipt, concurrent publisher, forged self-consistent receipt outside protected state, and marker-embed build-source regression; cache-hit and dry-run context vectors run no source-aware Go commands; generation is deterministic, go test ./tools/generate-vectors passes, and existing script-fixture and registry expected hashes remain unchanged.","[""TASK-260720-37ei85""]","[""TASK-260720-cw39jh""]","[{""text"":""Generate the separate Go build fixture and all positive identity, context, process, cache, and dry-run vectors"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Cover every minimum rejection cluster from the accepted research contract with named expected outcomes"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Prove existing script-fixture and registry expected hashes are unchanged and regeneration is deterministic"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Generate byte-level build-source and toolchain edge cases plus the legacy NUL-stream collision vector"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Code written per task description and AC"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Lint clean"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken"",""done"":true},{""text"":""New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Implementation matches AC"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Solution fits project architecture"",""done"":true},{""text"":""Tests green"",""done"":true},{""text"":""If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches"",""done"":false}]","Orchestrator integration precondition: create a task-scoped curator-spec worktree from origin/main 57c1f568 and bring forward only the complete accepted product diff from /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-37ei85/worktree. Exclude .temp, binaries, task-board config, alternate indexes, virtualenvs, and unrelated files. Treat that worktree as the authoritative composite rc.4 baseline. Do not commit or stage. Record predecessor source, frozen script-fixture/registry hashes, vector coverage mapping, and deterministic verification in outcome evidence.
