.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-31nl14/TASK-260720-31nl14_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:12398:The state model is now fixed: `preparing → prepared → committing → cleanup`, with `rolling_back → rollback_cleanup` on failure. Each target persists `pending → backed_up → committed`; rollback handles crashes that occur between a rename and its state write by inspecting deterministic sibling paths and hashes. Cleanup is itself journaled, so backups are never discarded until every consumer target is durable.
